profile.comment=Lightest first. Low: floodfill light only. Medium: traced light shadows (partial blocks and entities included) and hand light rays. High (Fastest) / High (Fast): the High look with lower internal resolutions and fewer samples, filled in by temporal accumulation and denoising. High (default): contact shadows, RSM GI, more light traces, DoF. Ultra: SSGI, more samples. Extreme (Lite): voxel GI and voxel reflections with the Ultra ranges and resolutions. Extreme (Balanced): Extreme at half resolution for light tracing, GI, clouds and volumetric light. Extreme: voxel GI and full resolution everything. Clouds look the same from Medium up; only their cost changes.

