option.LOOK_LUT_STRENGTH.comment=How much of the LUT is applied (mixed with the original color)
screen.LOOK_CUSTOM=Custom Look
screen.LOOK_CUSTOM.comment=Only used when Look is Custom. Sets the values that only the presets have. Everything else uses the regular options (Saturation, Contrast, ...)
option.LOOK_C_SKY_AMBIENT=Sky Ambient Strength
option.LOOK_C_SKY_AMBIENT.comment=Strength of the sky light that fills the shade. Lower values increase the difference between sun and shade (the sky itself keeps its brightness). Natural 1, Vivid 0.8
option.LOOK_C_SKY_SATURATION=Sky Color Saturation
option.LOOK_C_SKY_SATURATION.comment=How deep the sky blue is (both the sky and the sky ambient light). Natural 1, Vivid 1.08
option.LOOK_C_SUN_WARMTH=Sunlight Warmth
option.LOOK_C_SUN_WARMTH.comment=How much the direct sunlight is shifted toward warm colors (brightness is kept). Splits the warm sun from the blue sky light in the shade. The sky, clouds and sun disc keep their colors. 1 = a 5000K color against 6500K. Natural 0, Vivid 0.85
option.LOOK_C_BOUNCE=Bounce Light Strength
option.LOOK_C_BOUNCE.comment=Strength of the bounce light (light from surfaces hit by GI rays). The sky light is unchanged, so only the bounce from grass and walls gets stronger. GI Strength multiplies this. Natural 1, Vivid 1.6
option.LOOK_C_BOUNCE_SATURATION=Bounce Light Saturation
option.LOOK_C_BOUNCE_SATURATION.comment=Saturation of the bounce light (light from surfaces hit by GI rays). Higher values tint shade, birch trunks and cave entrances green from the grass. Brightness is unchanged. Natural 1, Vivid 1.5
option.LOOK_C_HIGHLIGHT=Highlight Range
option.LOOK_C_HIGHLIGHT.comment=Widens the brightness differences above middle gray (the dark side is unchanged). Higher values let white clouds and sunlit surfaces reach near white. Natural 1.1, Vivid 1.6
option.LOOK_C_DARK_LIFT=Shadow Lift
option.LOOK_C_DARK_LIFT.comment=Brightness of the darkest tones after the tone map. AgX expects a display with a 2.2 power curve, but the output is re-encoded with the piecewise sRGB curve, so on 2.2 displays dark areas sink by 1-3 EV and crush to black. 1 restores them (midtones and highlights barely change). Natural 0, Vivid 0.5
option.LOOK_C_BLOOM_SPREAD=Bloom Spread
option.LOOK_C_BLOOM_SPREAD.comment=How far the glow around lights spreads. Lower values keep it close to the light so shade is not lifted by the glow. Natural 0.82, Vivid 0.75
option.LOOK_C_BLOOM_FOG_CLEAR=Clear-Weather Bloomy Fog
option.LOOK_C_BLOOM_FOG_CLEAR.comment=How much wide glow is applied to distant terrain in clear weather (1 in rain). Natural 0.35, Vivid 0.35

# Block lighting
option.VOXEL_VOLUME=Voxel Volume
option.VOXEL_VOLUME.comment=Size of the voxel area around the player used for colored light and light shadows. Larger costs more VRAM.
value.VOXEL_VOLUME.0=128x64x128
value.VOXEL_VOLUME.1=192x96x192
value.VOXEL_VOLUME.2=256x128x256
value.VOXEL_VOLUME.3=384x128x384
option.FLOODFILL=Colored Floodfill
option.FLOODFILL.comment=Colored light that spreads through voxels. Used as indirect light when light shadows are on.
option.FLOODFILL_STRENGTH=Floodfill Indirect Strength
option.FLOODFILL_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the floodfill bounce light when light source shadows are enabled.
option.BLOCKLIGHT_BOUNCE=Block Light Wall Bounce
option.BLOCKLIGHT_BOUNCE.comment=How much block light bounces off walls and picks up their color (a red room tints the light red). 0 = no bounce.
option.BLOCKLIGHT_BRIGHTNESS=Block Light Brightness
option.BLOCKLIGHT_WARMTH=Block Light Warmth
option.BLOCKLIGHT_WARMTH.comment=0 = neutral white fire light, 1 = warm orange like vanilla.
option.LIGHT_FLICKER=Light Flicker
option.LIGHT_FLICKER.comment=Subtle flicker on fire based lights.
option.DECORATIVE_BLOCK_LIGHTS=Mineral Block Glow
option.DECORATIVE_BLOCK_LIGHTS.comment=Lapis, emerald, diamond, gold, redstone and amethyst blocks. Off = vanilla, Glow Only = the surface glows without lighting its surroundings, Light Source = also emits a dim colored light with shadows.
value.DECORATIVE_BLOCK_LIGHTS.0=Off
value.DECORATIVE_BLOCK_LIGHTS.1=Glow Only
value.DECORATIVE_BLOCK_LIGHTS.2=Light Source
option.LIGHT_SHADOWS=Light Source Shadows
option.LIGHT_SHADOWS.comment=Ray traces the strongest nearby lights so blocks, players and entities cast shadows from placed lights.
option.LIGHT_SHADOW_STRENGTH=Placed Light Shadow Darkness
option.LIGHT_SHADOW_STRENGTH.comment=How dark the shadows cast by placed lights are, including dropped, burning and glowing entities. 0 = no shadows, 1 = full shadows.
option.LIGHT_TRACE_COUNT=Traced Lights per Pixel
option.LIGHT_TRACE_RES=Trace Resolution
option.LIGHT_TRACE_RES.comment=Resolution of the light shadow trace. Lower is faster but noisier.
value.LIGHT_TRACE_RES.1=Full
value.LIGHT_TRACE_RES.2=Half
value.LIGHT_TRACE_RES.4=Quarter
option.LIGHT_SHAPE_TRACE=Block Shape Occlusion
option.LIGHT_SHAPE_TRACE.comment=Slabs, fences and walls cast shadows with their real shape.
option.LIGHT_SOURCE_SIZE=Light Source Size
option.LIGHT_SOURCE_SIZE.comment=Larger sources give softer shadow edges.
option.LIGHT_EMISSION_MASK_MODE=Emissive Face Shape
option.LIGHT_EMISSION_MASK_MODE.comment=How light-emitting blocks such as sea lanterns light nearby surfaces. Whole Face: the entire face glows evenly. Glowing Area: only the bright rectangle of the texture glows, so dark frames darken the contact line (no extra cost). Texture Mask: also follows the pattern inside the texture (heavier close to light blocks).
value.LIGHT_EMISSION_MASK_MODE.0=Whole Face
value.LIGHT_EMISSION_MASK_MODE.1=Glowing Area
value.LIGHT_EMISSION_MASK_MODE.2=Texture Mask
option.LIGHT_TRANSLUCENT_TINT=Stained Glass Tint
option.LIGHT_TRANSLUCENT_TINT.comment=Light passing through stained glass is colored.
option.LIGHT_SPECULAR=Block Light Specular
option.LIGHT_DENOISE=Light Denoiser
value.LIGHT_DENOISE.0=Off
value.LIGHT_DENOISE.1=Temporal
value.LIGHT_DENOISE.2=Temporal + Spatial
option.LIGHT_ENTITY_OCCLUSION=Entity Occlusion
option.LIGHT_ENTITY_OCCLUSION.comment=Mobs and block entities block placed light sources. Renders entities in the shadow pass (costly).
option.LIGHT_PLAYER_OCCLUSION=Player Occlusion
option.LIGHT_PLAYER_OCCLUSION.comment=Your player blocks placed light sources.
option.LIGHT_OCCLUSION_MODE=Entity Occlusion Method
option.LIGHT_OCCLUSION_MODE.comment=How players and mobs block light. Voxel: half-block boxes (fast, blocky shadows). Triangle: the actual model shape, including transparent parts.
value.LIGHT_OCCLUSION_MODE.0=Voxel
value.LIGHT_OCCLUSION_MODE.1=Triangle
option.LIGHT_ENTITY_TRIANGLES=Entity Triangle Limit
option.LIGHT_ENTITY_TRIANGLES.comment=Triangles kept for the Triangle method. 1024 are reserved for your player. Entities beyond the limit fall back to voxel boxes.
option.LIGHT_CONTACT_SHADOWS=Light Contact Shadows
option.LIGHT_CONTACT_SHADOWS.comment=Screen space shadows that add details too small for the voxel grid.
option.LIGHT_CULL_MODE=Light Selection Over Limit
option.LIGHT_CULL_MODE.comment=Which lights stay when a bin or the total light count is over its limit. Arrival Order: keeps the lights registered first; different lights drop out each frame and flicker. Nearest: keeps the closest lights. Brightness x Distance: keeps the lights that contribute the most (default). Nearest and Brightness x Distance fade lights at the cutoff over a few frames and align bins to the world grid, so the selection does not change as you walk. Scenes under the limits look and perform the same.
value.LIGHT_CULL_MODE.0=Arrival Order
value.LIGHT_CULL_MODE.1=Nearest
value.LIGHT_CULL_MODE.2=Brightness x Distance
option.LIGHT_MAX_COUNT=Total Light Limit
option.LIGHT_MAX_COUNT.comment=Lights handled as direct light per frame. Lights over the limit are dropped farthest first (their floodfill light stays). Higher costs more binning and tracing candidates. Matters for nether glowstone and light-heavy towns.
option.LIGHT_BIN_LIGHTS=Lights per Bin
option.LIGHT_BIN_LIGHTS.comment=Lights kept in one 8x8x8-block bin. Less important lights drop out beyond it. Higher makes pixels in dense light clusters check more lights. Above 64 uses about 10 MB more VRAM.
option.LIGHT_TRACE_STEPS=Light Shadow Ray Length
option.LIGHT_TRACE_STEPS.comment=Maximum blocks a light shadow ray walks. Too low cuts the shadows of long-reaching lights and leaks light. Most rays reach their light first, so raising it costs little.
option.LIGHT_SPECULAR_COUNT=Specular Lights
option.LIGHT_SPECULAR_COUNT.comment=Lights that add specular highlights per pixel (strongest first). Too few shows lines where highlights switch on floors lit by many lights. Higher costs more in opaque shading.
option.LIGHT_CONTACT_SHADOW_COUNT=Contact Shadow Lights
option.LIGHT_CONTACT_SHADOW_COUNT.comment=Lights that get screen-space contact shadows per pixel (strongest first). Higher is slower.
option.HAND_LIGHT=Handheld Light
option.HAND_LIGHT.comment=Holding a light source lights up the surroundings (both hands).
option.HAND_LIGHT_RAYS=Handheld Light Rays
option.HAND_LIGHT_RAYS.comment=Ray traced shadows for handheld lights.
option.HAND_LIGHT_SS_SHADOWS=Handheld Light Contact Shadows
option.HAND_LIGHT_SS_SHADOWS.comment=Screen space shadows from your hand and nearby entities.
option.HAND_LIGHT_BRIGHTNESS=Handheld Light Brightness
option.HAND_LIGHT_SHADOW_STRENGTH=Handheld Light Shadow Darkness
option.HAND_LIGHT_SHADOW_STRENGTH.comment=How dark the shadows cast by a handheld light are. 0 = no shadows. At 0.6 the direct shadow is full and some bounced light reaches it; above that only the bounced light shrinks, 1 = no bounce light from the handheld light.
option.ENTITY_LIGHTS=Entity Lights
option.ENTITY_LIGHTS.comment=Master switch for dynamic light from entities.
option.ITEM_LIGHTS=Dropped Item Lights
option.ITEM_LIGHTS.comment=Dropped light items (torches, lava buckets...) emit light.
option.PROJECTILE_LIGHTS=Projectile Lights
option.PROJECTILE_LIGHTS.comment=Spectral arrows, fireballs and fireworks emit light.
option.BURNING_ENTITY_LIGHTS=Burning Entity Lights
option.BURNING_ENTITY_LIGHTS.comment=Entities on fire emit light.
option.GLOWING_ENTITY_LIGHTS=Glowing Entity Lights
option.GLOWING_ENTITY_LIGHTS.comment=Blazes, glow squids, magma cubes, end crystals and flashing TNT emit light.

