option.MOON_SHADOW_STRENGTH=Moon Shadow Darkness
option.MOON_SHADOW_STRENGTH.comment=How dark the shadows cast by the moon and the End light are. 0 = no shadows, 1 = full shadows.
option.SHADOW_COLORED=Colored Shadows
option.SHADOW_COLORED.comment=Stained glass and water cast colored sun shadows.
option.ENTITY_SHADOWS=Entity Shadows
option.BLOCK_ENTITY_SHADOWS=Block Entity Shadows
option.SCREEN_SPACE_SHADOWS=Contact Shadows
option.AO_MODE=Ambient Occlusion
value.AO_MODE.0=Off
value.AO_MODE.1=SSAO
value.AO_MODE.2=GTAO
option.AO_STRENGTH=AO Strength
option.GI_MODE=Global Illumination
value.GI_MODE.0=Off
value.GI_MODE.1=RSM
value.GI_MODE.2=Screen Space
value.GI_MODE.3=Voxel Ray Traced
option.GI_SAMPLES=GI Samples
option.GI_STRENGTH=GI Strength
option.GI_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the bounce light (and, with screen-space or voxel ray tracing, the sky light). Higher values brighten shade, downward faces and rooms and reduce the contrast with sunlight. The effect is scaled per method so the same value looks similar (voxel x1, RSM x0.75, screen-space x0.5).
option.GI_MULTI_BOUNCE=Multiple Bounces
option.GI_MULTI_BOUNCE.comment=How much of the previous frame's GI is fed back into the surfaces GI rays hit, so light bounces again with every frame. Lets light reach deeper into cave entrances and rooms at almost no cost. 0 = single bounce, 1 = physically correct (screen-space and voxel ray tracing only).
option.GI_SKY_OCCLUSION=Sky Light Occlusion
option.GI_SKY_OCCLUSION.comment=How much of the sky light is occluded by the GI rays. 1 = light only comes from directions that see the sky (eaves, cave entrances and the back of rooms get darker, and openings show their direction). 0 = occlusion from the skylight level only (no direction, counted twice with the bounce). The default 0.5 keeps rooms and cave entrances from getting too dark (at 1 they are too dark even with multiple bounces). Screen-space and voxel ray tracing only. Multiplies the Look preset value (1 with Natural)
option.GI_GROUND_REPLACE=Ground Bounce Replacement
option.GI_GROUND_REPLACE.comment=How much of the gray ground bounce built into the sky ambient is replaced by the real ground color picked up by GI (green on grass). 1 = physically correct (shade and downward faces take the ground color and get darker). 0 = keeps the gray ground bounce (brighter, gray shade; the bounce is counted twice).
option.GI_RES=GI Resolution
value.GI_RES.1=Full
value.GI_RES.2=Half
option.GI_DENOISE=GI Denoiser
value.GI_DENOISE.0=Off
value.GI_DENOISE.1=Temporal
value.GI_DENOISE.2=Temporal + Spatial
option.GI_VOXEL_FADE=Voxel GI Fade Distance
option.GI_VOXEL_FADE.comment=Width in blocks over which voxel ray traced GI fades into the plain sky light at the edge of the voxel range. Wider hides the edge better when flying down from the sky or looking at distant terrain. Voxel ray tracing only.

