option.WATER_SEA_ABSORPTION=Sea Depth Tint
option.WATER_SEA_ABSORPTION.comment=Multiplier on light absorption in sea water. Higher: deep water turns dark and colored sooner and the bottom fades faster. Lower: clearer water you can see deeper into
option.WATER_LAKE_ABSORPTION=Lake Depth Tint
option.WATER_LAKE_ABSORPTION.comment=Multiplier on light absorption in lake water. Higher: deep water turns dark and colored sooner. Lower: clearer water
option.WATER_RIVER_ABSORPTION=River Depth Tint
option.WATER_RIVER_ABSORPTION.comment=Multiplier on light absorption in river water. Higher: deep water turns dark and colored sooner. Lower: clearer water
option.WATER_SEA_TURBIDITY=Sea Turbidity
option.WATER_SEA_TURBIDITY.comment=Multiplier on light scattering in sea water. Higher: milkier water that hides the bottom and glows with the water color. 0: no haze, only absorption
option.WATER_LAKE_TURBIDITY=Lake Turbidity
option.WATER_LAKE_TURBIDITY.comment=Multiplier on light scattering in lake water. Higher: milkier water that hides the bottom. 0: no haze, only absorption
option.WATER_RIVER_TURBIDITY=River Turbidity
option.WATER_RIVER_TURBIDITY.comment=Multiplier on light scattering in river water. Higher: milkier water that hides the bottom. 0: no haze, only absorption
option.WATER_RIPPLES=Ripples
option.WATER_RIPPLES.comment=Strength of the short waves (under 1 block)
option.WATER_FOAM=Foam
option.WATER_FOAM.comment=Whitecaps on breaking crests offshore. More with stronger wind. Not shown at the shoreline
option.WATER_LAKE_WAVES=Lake Wind
option.WATER_LAKE_WAVES.comment=Wind on lakes and ponds relative to the sea. Lakes also have a short fetch, so their waves stay small
option.WATER_RIVER_WAVES=River Wind
option.WATER_RIVER_WAVES.comment=Wind on rivers relative to the sea. Sloped flowing water also moves downstream
option.WATER_GLITTER=Water Glitter
option.WATER_GLITTER.comment=Draws the sun and moon mirrored by ripples smaller than a pixel as bright points that drift with the waves and thin out toward the edge of the path. Overall brightness stays about the same. Off keeps a smooth reflection. Slightly heavier
option.WATER_GLITTER_DENSITY=Glitter Amount
option.WATER_GLITTER_DENSITY.comment=Number of glitter points on the water. Higher: more, finer points packed close together. Lower: fewer, brighter points spread apart. Overall brightness stays the same. Needs Water Glitter
option.WATER_GLITTER_NIGHT_DENSITY=Night Glitter Amount
option.WATER_GLITTER_NIGHT_DENSITY.comment=Multiplier on the glitter amount while the moon is the light source. The moon path is far dimmer than the sun path, so lowering this leaves fewer points and gathers the same brightness into sparse white points. Overall brightness stays the same. Daytime is unchanged. Needs Water Glitter
option.WATER_GLITTER_LENGTH=Glitter Length
option.WATER_GLITTER_LENGTH.comment=Length of the horizontal streaks that glitter points form. Higher: longer streaks. Lower: shorter, rounder lumps. Needs Water Glitter
option.WATER_GLITTER_SINGLE=Round Glitter
option.WATER_GLITTER_SINGLE.comment=Share of the brightest points that stay one round point instead of splitting into a horizontal streak. 0: every point is a streak. Higher: more round points. Needs Water Glitter
option.WATER_REFLECT_SCATTER=Sea Reflection Blur
option.WATER_REFLECT_SCATTER.comment=How much waves smaller than a pixel blur the reflection of objects and sky on the sea. 0: a perfect mirror. Higher: reflections of distant trees and ice smear vertically and melt into the sky color. Calm water and water close to the camera stay mirrors. Needs Reflections set to SSR + Rough or higher
option.WATER_PARALLAX=Water Parallax
option.WATER_REFRACTION=Water Refraction
value.WATER_REFRACTION.0=Off
value.WATER_REFRACTION.1=Screen Space
value.WATER_REFRACTION.2=Ray Traced
option.WATER_REFRACTION_MODE=Refraction Method
option.WATER_REFRACTION_MODE.comment=Refraction of water seen from above. Waves Only: only the bending caused by waves (the bottom appears at its real depth; cheap). Edge Fade: full refraction, weakened toward the screen edges (the bottom slides near the edges). Voxel Traced: full refraction, and parts of the bottom that are not on screen are traced through voxels (the bottom looks shallower, like real water; off-screen parts use an approximate untextured color)
value.WATER_REFRACTION_MODE.0=Waves Only
value.WATER_REFRACTION_MODE.1=Edge Fade
value.WATER_REFRACTION_MODE.2=Voxel Traced
option.WATER_CAUSTICS=Water Caustics
option.WATER_TEXTURE=Vanilla Water Texture
option.WATER_FOG_DENSITY=Water Fog Density
option.WATER_FOG_DENSITY.comment=Multiplier on absorption and scattering of all water, on top of the sea / lake / river depth tint and turbidity. Affects both the view through the surface and the underwater fog
option.WATER_TYPE=Sea Water Color
value.WATER_TYPE.0=Open Ocean (Blue)
value.WATER_TYPE.1=Coastal (Green)
value.WATER_TYPE.2=Clear
option.WATER_TYPE.comment=Absorption and scattering of sea water. Affects both the view through the surface and the underwater fog
option.REFLECTIONS=Reflections
value.REFLECTIONS.0=Sky Only
value.REFLECTIONS.1=SSR
value.REFLECTIONS.2=SSR + Rough
value.REFLECTIONS.3=SSR + Voxel
option.SSR_STEPS=Reflection Steps
option.SPECULAR_SUN_STRENGTH=Sun Reflection Strength
option.SPECULAR_SUN_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the daytime sun reflected on water, puddles, glass and metal. 1 is the true mirror image of the sun disc, 0 shows no reflection
option.SPECULAR_MOON_STRENGTH=Moon Reflection Strength
option.SPECULAR_MOON_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the moon (and the End light) reflected at night. 1 is the true mirror image of the moon disc drawn in the sky, 0 shows no reflection. Higher values brighten the glint on rough surfaces such as iron blocks and stone, and the moon path on wavy water (only the center of a mirror-smooth surface never gets brighter than the disc)
option.SPECULAR_BLOCK_STRENGTH=Light Source Reflection Strength
option.SPECULAR_BLOCK_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of placed, held and item light sources reflected on surfaces. 1 is the true mirror image of the light, 0 shows no reflection
option.SPECULAR_SPARKLE=Reflection Sparkle
option.SPECULAR_SPARKLE.comment=Keeps the blown-out part of sun and light reflections on water, glass and metal intact so bloom and lens effects pick it up. Off lets anti-aliasing weaken small highlights

# Sky
option.ATMOSPHERE_MODE=Atmosphere
value.ATMOSPHERE_MODE.0=Analytic
value.ATMOSPHERE_MODE.1=Physical (LUT)
option.SUN_BRIGHTNESS=Sun Brightness
option.MOON_BRIGHTNESS=Moon Brightness
option.SKY_BRIGHTNESS=Sky Brightness
option.SKY_AMBIENT_SATURATION=Sky Ambient Saturation
option.SKY_AMBIENT_SATURATION.comment=How colorful the sky light that fills the shade is. Higher values make shade bluer against the warm sunlight. 0.3 = a subtle tint, 1 = the full sky color (shaded snow turns quite blue). Multiplies the Look preset value (1 with Natural)
option.SUN_MOON_STYLE=Sun & Moon
option.SUN_MOON_STYLE.comment=Vanilla = the game's sun and moon textures. Round = a round sun and a plain round moon that shows only the phase. Real Moon = a round sun and the moon drawn from NASA photographs of each phase (maria and craters). The moon's brightness, glint on water, flare and cloud shadows are the same as Round
value.SUN_MOON_STYLE.0=Vanilla
value.SUN_MOON_STYLE.1=Round
value.SUN_MOON_STYLE.2=Real Moon
option.STARS=Stars
option.TWILIGHT_STRETCH=Twilight Length
option.TWILIGHT_STRETCH.comment=Makes the colors of dawn and dusk last longer by compressing how far the sun sinks below the horizon, for the sky only. Civil twilight lasts about 20 seconds in Minecraft. 1 = real length. The sun disk, sunlight and shadows are unchanged

# Clouds
option.CLOUDS=Clouds
value.CLOUDS.0=Off
value.CLOUDS.1=Vanilla
value.CLOUDS.2=Volumetric 2D
value.CLOUDS.3=Volumetric 3D
option.CLOUD_QUALITY=Cloud Quality
option.CLOUD_QUALITY.comment=Ray march step counts. The shape and shading of the clouds are the same at every level; higher levels have less noise and cost more
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.0=Low
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.1=Medium
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.2=High
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.3=Ultra
option.CLOUD_RES=Cloud Resolution
value.CLOUD_RES.1=Full
value.CLOUD_RES.2=Half
value.CLOUD_RES.4=Quarter
option.CLOUD_TEMPORAL=Temporal Upscaling
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE=Cloud Coverage
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE.comment=Multiplier for all cloud layers. The actual amount also changes with the daily weather, time of day and rain
option.CLOUD_SCALE=Cloud Scale
option.CLOUD_SCALE.comment=Horizontal size multiplier for all clouds, shared by every height template
option.CLOUD_HEIGHT_PRESET=Cloud Height Template
option.CLOUD_HEIGHT_PRESET.comment=Maps real cloud heights onto the world. Vanilla: cumulus base y 165, cumulonimbus tops and cirrus near y 280-300. Tall World: base y 525, tops near y 1800. Realistic: 1 block = 1 m (base 1500, cirrus 8-10 km). Custom: the altitude and thickness sliders in each layer screen. Upper layers are compressed more than low clouds so cumulus keep a natural shape
value.CLOUD_HEIGHT_PRESET.0=Vanilla (-64 to 320)
value.CLOUD_HEIGHT_PRESET.1=Tall World (~2000)
value.CLOUD_HEIGHT_PRESET.2=Realistic (1 block = 1 m)
value.CLOUD_HEIGHT_PRESET.3=Custom
option.CLOUD_STYLE=Cloud Style
option.CLOUD_STYLE.comment=Picks the shape, density and lighting of the low clouds and the fair-weather amount of each layer. The cloud settings below multiply the style's values. Rain and thunderstorm clouds look nearly the same in every style except Vanilla Shape. Ray: lobed cumulus with blue sky between clumps. Bliss-like: smaller scattered clumps with frayed edges and deep shading. Vanilla Shape: flat slab clouds of uniform thickness with slightly rounded corners at the vanilla cloud height, pattern (vanilla or resource pack cloud texture) and drift, on a grid twice the vanilla 12 blocks (24). Mid and high clouds, cirrus and cumulonimbus are not drawn, and cloud amount, size, wind and height template do not change them. In rain and thunderstorms the gaps fill with cloud until the sky is almost covered, and the clouds darken and thicken. They are lighter than the Ray style. Realistic: density close to measured cumulus, crisp outlines. Cotton Candy: soft round clouds with a wide hazy edge. Towering Cumulus: tall white cumulus standing apart. Sparse Fair-Weather: small flat cumulus scattered over a wide blue sky. Stratocumulus Overcast: flat clumps covering most of the sky. Custom: set in "Custom Cloud Style"
value.CLOUD_STYLE.0=Custom
value.CLOUD_STYLE.1=Ray
value.CLOUD_STYLE.2=Bliss-like
value.CLOUD_STYLE.3=Vanilla Shape
value.CLOUD_STYLE.4=Realistic
value.CLOUD_STYLE.5=Cotton Candy
value.CLOUD_STYLE.6=Towering Cumulus
value.CLOUD_STYLE.7=Sparse Fair-Weather
value.CLOUD_STYLE.8=Stratocumulus Overcast
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_THICKNESS=Thickness
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_THICKNESS.comment=Thickness in blocks of the vanilla-shaped cloud slab, the same for every cell. The base stays at the vanilla cloud height and the cloud grows upward. A thicker cloud shows clearer side faces and a shaded base from below
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_COUNT=Upper Tiers
value.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_COUNT.0=None
value.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_COUNT.1=Middle
value.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_COUNT.2=Middle and High
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_COUNT.comment=Stacks tiers of blocky clouds above the vanilla-shaped clouds, made from the same pattern turned, shifted and thinned. Middle: a thin layer of scaly grains. High: a layer of long thin streaks. Each tier drifts in its own direction and speed, and is hidden from below a rain deck. Costs about 0.5 ms with both tiers
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_COVERAGE=Upper Tier Coverage
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_COVERAGE.comment=Share of the pattern cells kept in the upper tiers. Lower values leave sparser grains. The high tier keeps 0.8 times the middle tier's share
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_HEIGHT=Upper Tier Height
value.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_HEIGHT.0=High
value.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_HEIGHT.1=Below Build Limit
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_HEIGHT.comment=High: the middle tier is about 190 blocks and the high tier about 410 blocks above the clouds, so the tiers stand far apart and give depth. Below Build Limit: about 70 and 120 blocks above, so you can fly up between the tiers. Thunderstorm towers and anvils are lowered to match
option.CLOUD_S_SHAPE=Shape
option.CLOUD_S_SHAPE.comment=Cumulus: 3D clouds built from stacked lobes. Vanilla Shape: soft volumetric clouds placed like the vanilla clouds (in fair weather about 10% of the Ray style cost)
value.CLOUD_S_SHAPE.0=Cumulus
value.CLOUD_S_SHAPE.1=Vanilla Shape
option.CLOUD_S_HEIGHT=Cumulus Height
option.CLOUD_S_HEIGHT.comment=Multiplier for how tall cumulus grow. Higher gives towering cumulus, lower gives flat fair-weather cumulus
option.CLOUD_S_CONVECTION=Convection
option.CLOUD_S_CONVECTION.comment=Higher lets cumulus develop more and spread into stratocumulus less
option.CLOUD_S_TYPE_SHIFT=Cloud Type Shift
option.CLOUD_S_TYPE_SHIFT.comment=Shifts fair-weather clouds toward stratocumulus (negative) or cumulus (positive)
option.CLOUD_S_SPACING=Cloud Spacing
option.CLOUD_S_SPACING.comment=Size of the clear gap around large clouds. Higher removes small clouds and opens space between clumps
option.CLOUD_S_LOBES=Lobes
option.CLOUD_S_LOBES.comment=Depth of the lobes carved into the cloud surface. 0 gives smooth round clumps
option.CLOUD_S_BASE_RAGGED=Ragged Base
option.CLOUD_S_BASE_RAGGED.comment=Size of the bumps on the cloud base. 0 gives a flat base
option.CLOUD_S_LOBE_SHADE=Lobe Shading
option.CLOUD_S_LOBE_SHADE.comment=Depth of the shadow under each lobe. Higher increases the contrast between sunlit and shaded lobes
option.CLOUD_S_MULTISCATTER=Sunlit Brightness
option.CLOUD_S_MULTISCATTER.comment=Multiplier for light scattered many times inside the cloud. Higher makes the sunlit side whiter and the shaded side brighter
option.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET=Cloud Climate
option.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET.comment=Which cloud types appear and how often, with day-to-day changes. Temperate: cumulus and cirrus, stratocumulus on humid days. Tropical: afternoon towering cumulus and distant cumulonimbus. Arid: few small clouds. Polar: low stratus decks and ice clouds. Maritime: wide stratocumulus and puffy cumulus. Custom: the Climate sliders in each layer screen
value.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET.0=Temperate
value.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET.1=Tropical
value.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET.2=Arid
value.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET.3=Polar
value.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET.4=Maritime
value.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET.5=Custom
option.CLOUD_ALTITUDE=Low Cloud Altitude
option.CLOUD_ALTITUDE.comment=Custom height template only. World y of the low cloud base
option.CLOUD_THICKNESS=Low Cloud Thickness
option.CLOUD_THICKNESS.comment=Custom height template only. Blocks for the cumulus layer (real 4.5 km). Also sets the scale of every layer left on automatic
option.CLOUD_C_LOW=Climate: Low Cloud Amount
option.CLOUD_C_LOW.comment=Custom climate only. Average low cloud cover (varies by day)
option.CLOUD_C_CONVECTION=Climate: Convection
option.CLOUD_C_CONVECTION.comment=Custom climate only. How tall cumulus grow on sunny afternoons
option.CLOUD_C_STRATUS=Climate: Stratocumulus
option.CLOUD_C_STRATUS.comment=Custom climate only. How often clouds spread into flat layers on humid days and at night
option.CLOUD_C_MID=Climate: Mid Cloud Amount
option.CLOUD_C_HIGH=Climate: High Cloud Amount
option.CLOUD_C_STORMS=Climate: Fair Weather Storms
option.CLOUD_C_STORMS.comment=Custom climate only. Chance of distant cumulonimbus on unstable afternoons (thunderstorms always make them)
option.CLOUD_CUMULONIMBUS=Cumulonimbus
option.CLOUD_CUMULONIMBUS.comment=Thunderstorm towers with anvils, overshooting tops, mammatus and rain shafts. Not drawn by the vanilla-shaped clouds. Only costs while storms exist
option.CLOUD_SPEED=Cloud Speed
option.CLOUD_MULTISCATTER=Multiple Scattering Octaves
option.CLOUD_MULTISCATTER.comment=How many octaves the multiple scattering is split into. With fewer octaves the rest is folded into the last one, so the brightness stays about the same; more octaves cost more
option.CLOUD_CIRRUS=High Clouds
option.CLOUD_CIRRUS.comment=Thin translucent ice clouds around 9 km: cirrus tufts with sheared fall streaks, cirrocumulus ripples and cirrostratus veils (faint 22 degree halo)
option.CLOUD_CIRRUS_COVERAGE=High Cloud Amount
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS=Cloud Shadows
option.CLOUD_INTERIOR_VISIBILITY=Visibility Inside Clouds
option.CLOUD_INTERIOR_VISIBILITY.comment=Distance in blocks at which things are veiled down to 5% while you stand inside a cloud (a smaller value is thicker). The fog grows with distance and only fills the cloud: sight lines that leave the cloud (through the top or bottom of a vanilla-shaped slab) are not veiled beyond that point. It is thin at the cloud's edge, thickens over several to a dozen blocks deeper in, and thins out the same way when you leave. Real cloud interiors close in white within tens of metres. 0 turns the effect off
option.CLOUD_LOW_COVERAGE=Low Cloud Coverage
option.CLOUD_LOW_COVERAGE.comment=Multiplier on the amount of cumulus, stratocumulus and rain clouds, on top of Cloud Coverage and the climate
option.CLOUD_LOW_DENSITY=Low Cloud Density
option.CLOUD_LOW_DENSITY.comment=Optical density of low clouds. The default 0.25 gives soft clouds with translucent edges, higher values give denser, more solid clouds. Rain and storm clouds scale with it. Shading (lit side and dark base) is kept at low values
option.CLOUD_LOW_SCALE=Low Cloud Size
option.CLOUD_LOW_SCALE.comment=Horizontal size multiplier for low clouds only (on top of Cloud Scale)
option.CLOUD_LOW_EROSION=Low Cloud Erosion
option.CLOUD_LOW_EROSION.comment=How strongly billows and wisps cut into the edges. Lower gives smooth cotton, higher gives cauliflower tops and ragged bases
option.CLOUD_LOW_WIND=Low Wind Speed
option.CLOUD_LOW_WIND.comment=m/s at the low cloud level (multiplied by Cloud Speed)
option.CLOUD_LOW_WIND_ANGLE=Low Wind Direction
option.CLOUD_LOW_WIND_ANGLE.comment=Degrees the clouds move towards. 0 = east (+X), 90 = south (+Z)
option.CLOUD_FRACTUS=Thin Fragments
option.CLOUD_FRACTUS.comment=Thin torn wisps scattered in loose groups around the main clouds. 0 turns them off
option.CLOUD_MID_ALTITUDE=Mid Cloud Altitude
option.CLOUD_MID_ALTITUDE.comment=Custom height template only. World y of the mid cloud base. 0 = automatic (real proportions above the low clouds)
option.CLOUD_MID_THICKNESS=Mid Cloud Thickness
option.CLOUD_MID_THICKNESS.comment=Custom height template only. Blocks. 0 = automatic (real 900 m)
option.CLOUD_MID_COVERAGE=Mid Cloud Coverage
option.CLOUD_MID_COVERAGE.comment=Multiplier on the amount of altocumulus and altostratus
option.CLOUD_MID_DENSITY=Mid Cloud Density
option.CLOUD_MID_SCALE=Mid Cloud Size
option.CLOUD_MID_EROSION=Mid Cloud Erosion
option.CLOUD_MID_EROSION.comment=Lower gives smooth rounded patches, higher breaks them into small ragged lumps
option.CLOUD_MID_WIND=Mid Wind Speed
option.CLOUD_MID_WIND.comment=m/s at the mid cloud level (multiplied by Cloud Speed)
option.CLOUD_MID_WIND_ANGLE=Mid Wind Direction
option.CLOUD_MID_WIND_ANGLE.comment=Degrees the clouds move towards. 0 = east (+X), 90 = south (+Z)
option.CLOUD_HIGH_ALTITUDE=High Cloud Altitude
option.CLOUD_HIGH_ALTITUDE.comment=Custom height template only. World y of the bottom of the cirrus layer. 0 = automatic (real 8.4 km)
option.CLOUD_HIGH_THICKNESS=High Cloud Thickness
option.CLOUD_HIGH_THICKNESS.comment=Custom height template only. Blocks. 0 = automatic (real 1.4 km)
option.CLOUD_HIGH_DENSITY=High Cloud Density
option.CLOUD_HIGH_DENSITY.comment=Opacity of cirrus, cirrocumulus and cirrostratus
option.CLOUD_HIGH_SCALE=High Cloud Size
option.CLOUD_HIGH_WIND=High Wind Speed
option.CLOUD_HIGH_WIND.comment=m/s at the cirrus level (multiplied by Cloud Speed)
option.CLOUD_HIGH_WIND_ANGLE=High Wind Direction
option.CLOUD_HIGH_WIND_ANGLE.comment=Degrees. Cirrus streaks line up with this direction
option.CLOUD_CB_HEIGHT=Cumulonimbus Top
option.CLOUD_CB_HEIGHT.comment=Custom height template only. World y of the anvil top. 0 = automatic (real 10.2 km)
option.CLOUD_CB_COVERAGE=Storm Cells
option.CLOUD_CB_COVERAGE.comment=How many cumulonimbus cells form in thunderstorms and on stormy afternoons
option.CLOUD_CB_DENSITY=Cumulonimbus Density
option.CLOUD_CB_ANVIL=Anvil Length
option.CLOUD_CB_ANVIL.comment=How far the anvil spreads downwind. 0 keeps it over the tower
option.CLOUD_CB_RAIN_SHAFTS=Rain Shafts
option.CLOUD_CB_RAIN_SHAFTS.comment=Density of the grey rain curtains under storm cores. 0 turns them off
option.CLOUD_EDGE_SOFTNESS=Edge Softness
option.CLOUD_EDGE_SOFTNESS.comment=Width of the thin, soft margin of low clouds. Higher looks fluffier, lower looks crisper
option.CLOUD_EDGE_HAZE=Edge Haze
option.CLOUD_EDGE_HAZE.comment=Thin haze spreading out from the edges of fair-weather cumulus. 0 gives crisp outlines
option.CLOUD_CORE_STRENGTH=Core Density
option.CLOUD_CORE_STRENGTH.comment=Density of the centres of fair-weather cumulus bodies (small fragments and small clouds get half). Higher looks more solid with deeper shading between the lobes. 0.25 gives thin cores, 2.0 and above is almost uniformly dense
option.CLOUD_SILVER_LINING=Silver Lining
option.CLOUD_SILVER_LINING.comment=Glow of cloud edges backlit by the sun or moon
option.CLOUD_POWDER=Dark Edges
option.CLOUD_POWDER.comment=Darkening of thin edges with the sun behind you (powder effect)
option.CLOUD_AMBIENT=Sky Light in Clouds
option.CLOUD_AMBIENT.comment=Blue sky light inside clouds. Higher lifts the shaded sides
option.CLOUD_BASE_SHADE=Base Darkness
option.CLOUD_BASE_SHADE.comment=How grey the bottoms of thick clouds get
option.CLOUD_DRAW_DISTANCE=Cloud Draw Distance
option.CLOUD_DRAW_DISTANCE.comment=Kilometres at real scale for low and mid clouds. Shorter is faster
option.CLOUD_C_MID.comment=Custom climate only. Average amount of altocumulus and altostratus (varies by day)
option.CLOUD_C_HIGH.comment=Custom climate only. Average amount of cirrus (varies by day)

# Fog
option.FOG_STYLE=Fog Style
option.FOG_STYLE.comment=Shape and balance of the fog layers. Ray: physically based, a haze layer with a flat top, morning fog banks and valley mist. Bliss-like: denser haze and distance fade, more fog banks, mist also in the evening and at night, and a strong glow on the sun side. Nostalgia-like: no fog bank, haze that thins out gradually with height, a light distance fade, mist only in the morning and in rain. Custom: the sliders in Custom Fog Style. Distant air always fades into the horizon sky of the same direction. Overall strength is set by Fog Density and the Look preset
value.FOG_STYLE.0=Ray (Physical)
value.FOG_STYLE.1=Bliss-like
value.FOG_STYLE.2=Nostalgia-like
value.FOG_STYLE.3=Custom
screen.FOG_STYLE_SCREEN=Custom Fog Style
option.FOG_C_HAZE=Haze
option.FOG_C_HAZE.comment=Custom style only. Multiplies the haze density
option.FOG_C_EDGE=Distance Fade
option.FOG_C_EDGE.comment=Custom style only. Optical depth of the haze at the edge of the render distance. 0.6 leaves about 55% of the terrain visible, higher fades the distance more
option.FOG_C_LAYER=Fog Layer
option.FOG_C_LAYER.comment=Custom style only. Multiplies the density of the mid-level fog layer
option.FOG_C_GROUND=Ground Mist
option.FOG_C_GROUND.comment=Custom style only. Multiplies the density of the ground mist
option.FOG_C_FORWARD=Sunlit Glow
option.FOG_C_FORWARD.comment=Custom style only. How brightly sunlit haze and fog glow toward the sun (multiplies Light Shaft Strength)
option.FOG_BIOME=Biome Fog
option.FOG_BIOME.comment=Swamps and jungles get more fog and mist, deserts and badlands only dusty haze, snowy biomes thinner haze, oceans less valley mist
option.FOG_DENSITY=Fog Density
option.FOG_DENSITY.comment=Multiplies the Look preset value (1 with Natural)
option.FOG_HEIGHT_PRESET=Fog Height Template
option.FOG_HEIGHT_PRESET.comment=Heights of the haze, the mid-level fog layer and the ground mist for worlds of different height. Vanilla: haze up to y 143 at noon, fog layer y 70-105, mist up to y 71. Tall World: haze up to y 406, fog layer y 90-200. Realistic: 1 block = 1 m (haze 1.1 km, fog layer 100-440 m). Custom: the sliders in Fog Heights. Match Clouds: follows the Cloud Height Template (the haze top stays at 3/4 of the cloud base)
value.FOG_HEIGHT_PRESET.0=Vanilla (-64 to 320)
value.FOG_HEIGHT_PRESET.1=Tall World (~2000)
value.FOG_HEIGHT_PRESET.2=Realistic (1 block = 1 m)
value.FOG_HEIGHT_PRESET.3=Custom
value.FOG_HEIGHT_PRESET.4=Match Clouds
screen.FOG_HEIGHT_SCREEN=Fog Heights
option.FOG_C_SEA_LEVEL=Sea Level
option.FOG_C_SEA_LEVEL.comment=Custom template only. The height the haze and fog are measured from
option.FOG_C_HAZE_TOP=Haze Top
option.FOG_C_HAZE_TOP.comment=Custom template only. Top of the haze at noon (lower in the morning and at night). 0 = 3/4 of the cloud base
option.FOG_C_LAYER_BASE=Fog Layer Base
option.FOG_C_LAYER_BASE.comment=Custom template only. Bottom of the mid-level fog layer
option.FOG_C_LAYER_THICKNESS=Fog Layer Thickness
option.FOG_C_LAYER_THICKNESS.comment=Custom template only
option.FOG_LAYER=Fog Layer
option.FOG_LAYER.comment=Patches of fog at mid height (y 70-105 in Vanilla) with a flat top. Most common in the morning and on humid days, and spreads wide in rain. Light shafts show best inside it. Slightly heavier
option.FOG_MIST=Ground Mist
option.FOG_MIST.comment=Radiation fog that pools in valleys and over water at night, peaks at dawn and burns off about two hours after sunrise. Thicker on clear, humid days and after rain
option.FOG_MIST_ALTITUDE=Mist Altitude
option.FOG_MIST_ALTITUDE.comment=Custom template only. Top of the ground mist
option.VL=Volumetric Light
option.VL_SAMPLES=Volumetric Samples
option.VL_RES=Volumetric Resolution
value.VL_RES.1=Full
value.VL_RES.2=Half
value.VL_RES.4=Quarter
option.VL_STRENGTH=Light Shaft Strength
option.VL_COLORED_SHADOWS=Colored Light Shafts
option.FOG_BLOCKLIGHT=Block Light Fog
option.FOG_BLOCKLIGHT.comment=Torches and other lights illuminate the fog.
option.FOG_BLOCKLIGHT_STRENGTH=Block Light Fog Strength
option.FOG_CLOUD_SHADOWS=Cloud Shadowed Light Shafts
option.VL_FAR=Distant Light Shafts
option.VL_FAR.comment=Light shafts beyond the shadow distance, traced in screen space from hills, trees and buildings. Only matters when the render distance is longer than the shadow distance. Slightly heavier
option.CAVE_LEAK_PREVENTION=Cave Light Leak Prevention
