# Lens
option.LENS_GLOW_STRENGTH=Overall Glow Strength
option.LENS_GLOW_STRENGTH.comment=Strengthens or weakens every effect that spreads light around bright things at once. 1 = unchanged, 0 = all off, 2 = double. Covers: bloom, bloom fog, point spread (blown-out specular points), sun / moon flare (ghosts, starburst, halo, glare, dirt, streak), ghosts and starbursts from bright pixels, veiling glare, spherical aberration glow, halation and the bright rim of bokeh balls. It multiplies each effect's own strength. Point spread keeps the total light and only scales the share that is spread (at most all of the point's light)
option.LENS_FLARE=Lens Flare
option.LENS_FLARE.comment=Master switch for the sun / moon flare (ghosts, starburst, halo, glare, dirt, streak)
option.LENS_FLARE_STRENGTH=Flare Strength
option.LENS_FLARE_STRENGTH.comment=Works with every lens. 1 = as designed (ghosts use physically computed reflectance)
option.LENS_POINT_SPREAD_STRENGTH=Point Spread Strength
option.LENS_POINT_SPREAD_STRENGTH.comment=Specular highlights brighter than white (sun glints on water, metal, glass) get a lens point-spread glow: the brighter the point, the larger it looks, like a point light. Total light is unchanged. Scales with the lens's veiling glare. 0 = off. Needs Reflection Sparkle. Costs about 0.2 ms
option.LENS_POINT_SPREAD_SIZE=Point Spread Size
option.LENS_POINT_SPREAD_SIZE.comment=Size of the glow around blown-out reflection points (about 1-2 px Small, 3-5 px Medium, 4-8 px Large, 7-10 px Extra Large). Larger glows merge neighboring glints and wave surfaces into one lump and look hazier. Strength sets how much light goes into the glow. Needs Reflection Sparkle
value.LENS_POINT_SPREAD_SIZE.0=Small
value.LENS_POINT_SPREAD_SIZE.1=Medium
value.LENS_POINT_SPREAD_SIZE.2=Large
value.LENS_POINT_SPREAD_SIZE.3=Extra Large
option.LENS_PRESET=Lens
option.LENS_PRESET.comment=Picks the lens character (flare colors and shapes, starburst rays, aberrations). Individual strengths only apply with Custom (see Custom Lens). Toggles always apply. Sonnar and later are computed from the patent prescriptions of real lenses. Sonnar = high contrast, few ghosts, slight pincushion. Summilux 35 = glow wide open, cat's eye bokeh, dark corners. Canon 50/1.2 = soft and low contrast wide open, background smears toward the edges, strong corner falloff. Hologon = straight lines across 110 degrees, strong corner falloff, fixed f/8 (FOV 68). Flektogon = wavy mustache distortion (FOV 54). Fish-eye = fisheye projection, straight lines bend (FOV 110, Fisheye Framing = Fit Width matches the real lens). Gyogyotto = near-orthographic fisheye, edges squeezed harder than the Rokkor, fixed f/8. Ultra Wide-Heliar 12 = 121 degrees, plain barrel distortion, very dark corners even stopped down. New FD 14 = 114 degrees, barrel distortion that eases off at the corners, dark corners wide open that recover when stopped down. STF 135 = apodization filter, out-of-focus highlights melt away without a rim. FA 28 Soft = soft focus halo wide open that disappears by f/5.6 (set the aperture with Depth of Field). Canon 50/0.95 = the darkest corners, glow only wide open. The FOV in a lens name fits the 36 mm width of the 35 mm frame to the screen width: vertical FOV = 2 atan(18 / f x 9 / 16) (35 mm = 32, 20 mm = 54, 15 mm = 68). 50 mm and longer would need less than the game's minimum, so use 30 (still wider than the real lens)
